# HECTOR is an alpha. This file describes the alpha pre-release below; the Zenodo DOI is added
# at the first full release (docs/release.md).
# Contributor roles (CRediT) are in CREDITS.md: CFF has no field for them.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  HECTOR is an alpha: please do not cite it until its first full release, and then cite that
  release's DOI. Alpha pre-releases (this is v2026.10-alpha.1) promise nothing persistent. Contributor roles (CRediT) are listed in CREDITS.md.
type: dataset
version: "2026.10-alpha.1"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
title: "HECTOR: Historical Economic Commodities: Terminologies, Ontologies & Rates"
abstract: >-
  An open Linked Data vocabulary of historical traded commodities, the units they were
  measured and packed in, and the customs rates charged on them. Every record gathers the
  spellings the sources use, links to the Getty Art & Architecture Thesaurus and Wikidata
  where an equivalent exists, and is published as JSON-LD (with Turtle and RDF/XML) aligned
  with Linked Art. Its first content comes from the London customs accounts (1380-1560) and
  the English Books of Rates of 1507, 1545 and 1558, in Stuart Jenks's transcriptions.
  Developed within the project "Unlocking Upcycled Medieval Data: North Sea Networks,
  People, and Commodities in the London Customs Accounts 1380-1560", funded by the AHRC
  (AH/Z507179/1) and the DFG (project number 547507634).
authors:
  - family-names: Gadd
    given-names: Stephen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3060-0181"
    affiliation: "Institute of Historical Research, University of London"
url: "https://w3id.org/hector/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ihr-digital/hector"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - commodities
  - units of measure
  - customs
  - economic history
  - linked data
  - Linked Art
  - controlled vocabulary
references:
  - type: data
    title: London Customs Accounts 1380-1560
    authors:
      - family-names: Colson
        given-names: J.
      - family-names: Scheltjens
        given-names: W.
      - family-names: Benbow
        given-names: E.
      - family-names: Gadd
        given-names: S.
      - family-names: Grove-Gordillo
        given-names: M.
    url: "https://docuracy.github.io/London_Customs_Accounts/"
    notes: The glossary from which HECTOR's commodities and units are derived.
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Transcriptions of the London customs accounts and of the Tudor Books of Rates
      (unpublished transcript files)
    authors:
      - family-names: Jenks
        given-names: Stuart
    notes: >-
      Stuart Jenks's own transcript files, licensed by him under CC BY 4.0 as reproduced in
      HECTOR and for all data derived from them.
